{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const createQuery: {\n<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>  (options: UndefinedInitialDataOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>, queryClient?: () => QueryClient): UseQueryResult<TData, TError>;\n<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>  (options: DefinedInitialDataOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>, queryClient?: () => QueryClient): DefinedUseQueryResult<TData, TError>;\n} = useQuery;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/solid-query/src/index.ts#L57","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/solid-query/src/index.ts:57"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"call-signature","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call Signature"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>(options: UndefinedInitialDataOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>, queryClient?: () => QueryClient): UseQueryResult<TData, TError>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Subscribes to a query: a declarative dependency on an asynchronous source of data that is tied to a unique key.\nThe query runs when the options call for it — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled: false"},{"type":"text","value":" skips the initial fetch."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"tqueryfndata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TQueryFnData"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryFnData"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"terror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TError"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Error"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"tdata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TData"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryFnData"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"tquerykey","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TQueryKey"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" readonly "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":"[] = readonly "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":"[]"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/UndefinedInitialDataOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UndefinedInitialDataOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryFnData"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TError"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryKey"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An accessor returning the "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/UndefinedInitialDataOptions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"UndefinedInitialDataOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to use — everything you can\npass to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"queryclient","children":[{"type":"text","value":"queryClient?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"() => "},{"type":"link","href":"../classes/QueryClient.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An accessor for a custom "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":". Otherwise, the one from the nearest context\nwill be used."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/UseQueryResult.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseQueryResult"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TError"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The current query result, as a Solid store. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pending"},{"type":"text","value":" if there is no cached data to\ndisplay, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":" if the last fetch attempt failed, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"success"},{"type":"text","value":" if the query has data to display.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPending"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isSuccess"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isError"},{"type":"text","value":" are derived booleans for convenience."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"see","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../functions/queryOptions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"queryOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to share these options between "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" and imperative APIs like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryClient.query"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { For, Match, Switch } from 'solid-js'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Posts() {\n  const postsQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['posts'],\n    queryFn: fetchPosts,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Switch>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isPending}>Loading...</Match>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isError}>Error: {postsQuery.error.message}</Match>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isSuccess}>\n        <ul>\n          <For each={postsQuery.data}>{(post) => <li>{post.title}</li>}</For>\n        </ul>\n        <div>{postsQuery.isFetching ? 'Background Updating...' : ' '}</div>\n      </Match>\n    </Switch>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":" derives whatever "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" a component needs from the cached value, without changing what's\nactually stored in the cache — the cache still holds the full "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Post[]"},{"type":"text","value":", but "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" here is a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Match, Switch } from 'solid-js'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction PostCount() {\n  const postsQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['posts'],\n    queryFn: fetchPosts,\n    select: (posts) => posts.length,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Switch>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isPending}>Loading...</Match>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isError}>Error: {postsQuery.error.message}</Match>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isSuccess}>{postsQuery.data} posts</Match>\n    </Switch>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A dependent query, only enabled once "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"postId"},{"type":"text","value":" is set:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Match, Switch } from 'solid-js'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Post(props: { postId: number | undefined }) {\n  const postQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['post', props.postId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchPost(props.postId!),\n    enabled: props.postId != null,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Switch fallback={<h1>{postQuery.data?.title}</h1>}>\n      <Match when={props.postId == null}>Select a post</Match>\n      <Match when={postQuery.isLoading}>Loading...</Match>\n      <Match when={postQuery.isError}>Error: {postQuery.error.message}</Match>\n    </Switch>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same dependent query, using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skipToken"},{"type":"text","value":" to disable it in a type-safe way instead of relying on\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled"},{"type":"text","value":". The non-null assertion is still needed — Solid's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props"},{"type":"text","value":" narrowing doesn't survive into the\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":" closure the way a local "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"const"},{"type":"text","value":" would — but "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skipToken"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":"'s return type accurate\nwithout it. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"refetch"},{"type":"text","value":" doesn't work while "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skipToken"},{"type":"text","value":" — use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled: false"},{"type":"text","value":" instead if you\nneed to trigger the query manually:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Match, Switch } from 'solid-js'\nimport { skipToken, useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Post(props: { postId: number | undefined }) {\n  const postQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['post', props.postId],\n    queryFn: props.postId != null ? () => fetchPost(props.postId!) : skipToken,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Switch fallback={<h1>{postQuery.data?.title}</h1>}>\n      <Match when={props.postId == null}>Select a post</Match>\n      <Match when={postQuery.isLoading}>Loading...</Match>\n      <Match when={postQuery.isError}>Error: {postQuery.error.message}</Match>\n    </Switch>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Seeding a detail query from an already-cached list, to skip the loading state. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialDataUpdatedAt"},{"type":"text","value":" carries\nover the list's own fetch time, so that if you set a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"staleTime"},{"type":"text","value":", it's measured from when the list was\nfetched rather than from now:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useQuery, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Post(props: { postId: number }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n\n  const postQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['post', props.postId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchPost(props.postId),\n    initialData: () =>\n      queryClient\n        .getQueryData<Array<Post>>(['posts'])\n        ?.find((post) => post.id === props.postId),\n    initialDataUpdatedAt: () =>\n      queryClient.getQueryState(['posts'])?.dataUpdatedAt,\n  }))\n\n  return postQuery.isError ? <span>Error: {postQuery.error.message}</span> : <h1>{postQuery.data?.title}</h1>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paginated data, keeping the previous page's data visible while the next page loads:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { For, createSignal } from 'solid-js'\nimport { keepPreviousData, useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Posts() {\n  const [page, setPage] = createSignal(0)\n\n  const postsQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['posts', page()],\n    queryFn: () => fetchPosts(page()),\n    placeholderData: keepPreviousData,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <ul>\n        <For each={postsQuery.data}>{(post) => <li>{post.title}</li>}</For>\n      </ul>\n      <button\n        disabled={postsQuery.isPlaceholderData}\n        onClick={() => setPage((old) => old + 1)}\n      >\n        Next Page\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"call-signature-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call Signature"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>(options: DefinedInitialDataOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>, queryClient?: () => QueryClient): DefinedUseQueryResult<TData, TError>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Subscribes to a query: a declarative dependency on an asynchronous source of data that is tied to a unique key.\nThe query runs when the options call for it — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled: false"},{"type":"text","value":" skips the initial fetch."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This overload is selected when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialData"},{"type":"text","value":" is set, so the resulting "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" is never "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" (unless\na "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":" changes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":" to include "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"type-parameters-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"tqueryfndata-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TQueryFnData"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryFnData"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"terror-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TError"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Error"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"tdata-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TData"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryFnData"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"tquerykey-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TQueryKey"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" readonly "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":"[] = readonly "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":"[]"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parameters-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"options-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/DefinedInitialDataOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DefinedInitialDataOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryFnData"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TError"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryKey"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An accessor returning the "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/DefinedInitialDataOptions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DefinedInitialDataOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to use — everything you can\npass to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":", with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialData"},{"type":"text","value":" set."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"queryclient-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"queryClient?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"() => "},{"type":"link","href":"../classes/QueryClient.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An accessor for a custom "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":". Otherwise, the one from the nearest context\nwill be used."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"returns-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/DefinedUseQueryResult.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DefinedUseQueryResult"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TError"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The current query result, as a Solid store, typed so that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"success"},{"type":"text","value":" — or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":" if a\nfetch attempt fails while keeping the existing data ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" never resolves to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pending"},{"type":"text","value":" in this overload's\ntype, since "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialData"},{"type":"text","value":" guarantees data upfront). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isSuccess"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isError"},{"type":"text","value":" are derived booleans for\nconvenience."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"see-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../functions/queryOptions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"queryOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to share these options between "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" and imperative APIs like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryClient.query"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { For } from 'solid-js'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Posts() {\n  // `postsQuery.data` is never `undefined`, thanks to `initialData` — even if a refetch fails, so the\n  // list stays visible alongside the error.\n  const postsQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['posts'],\n    queryFn: fetchPosts,\n    initialData: [],\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {postsQuery.isError ? <span>Error: {postsQuery.error.message}</span> : null}\n      <ul>\n        <For each={postsQuery.data}>{(post) => <li>{post.title}</li>}</For>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"call-signature","text":"Call Signature","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":3},{"id":"tqueryfndata","text":"TQueryFnData","level":4},{"id":"terror","text":"TError","level":4},{"id":"tdata","text":"TData","level":4},{"id":"tquerykey","text":"TQueryKey","level":4},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":4},{"id":"queryclient","text":"queryClient?","level":4},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":3},{"id":"see","text":"See","level":3},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":3},{"id":"call-signature-2","text":"Call Signature","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters-2","text":"Type Parameters","level":3},{"id":"tqueryfndata-2","text":"TQueryFnData","level":4},{"id":"terror-2","text":"TError","level":4},{"id":"tdata-2","text":"TData","level":4},{"id":"tquerykey-2","text":"TQueryKey","level":4},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":3},{"id":"options-2","text":"options","level":4},{"id":"queryclient-2","text":"queryClient?","level":4},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":3},{"id":"see-2","text":"See","level":3},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nconst createQuery: {\n<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>  (options: UndefinedInitialDataOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>, queryClient?: () => QueryClient): UseQueryResult<TData, TError>;\n<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>  (options: DefinedInitialDataOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>, queryClient?: () => QueryClient): DefinedUseQueryResult<TData, TError>;\n} = useQuery;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/solid-query/src/index.ts:57](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/solid-query/src/index.ts#L57)\n\n## Call Signature\n\n```ts\n<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>(options: UndefinedInitialDataOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>, queryClient?: () => QueryClient): UseQueryResult<TData, TError>;\n```\n\nSubscribes to a query: a declarative dependency on an asynchronous source of data that is tied to a unique key.\nThe query runs when the options call for it — `enabled: false` skips the initial fetch.\n\n### Type Parameters\n\n#### TQueryFnData\n\n`TQueryFnData` = `unknown`\n\n#### TError\n\n`TError` = `Error`\n\n#### TData\n\n`TData` = `TQueryFnData`\n\n#### TQueryKey\n\n`TQueryKey` *extends* readonly `unknown`[] = readonly `unknown`[]\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### options\n\n[`UndefinedInitialDataOptions`](../type-aliases/UndefinedInitialDataOptions.md)\\<`TQueryFnData`, `TError`, `TData`, `TQueryKey`\\>\n\nAn accessor returning the [UndefinedInitialDataOptions](../type-aliases/UndefinedInitialDataOptions.md) to use — everything you can\npass to `useQuery`.\n\n#### queryClient?\n\n() => [`QueryClient`](../classes/QueryClient.md)\n\nAn accessor for a custom `QueryClient`. Otherwise, the one from the nearest context\nwill be used.\n\n### Returns\n\n[`UseQueryResult`](../type-aliases/UseQueryResult.md)\\<`TData`, `TError`\\>\n\nThe current query result, as a Solid store. `status` is `pending` if there is no cached data to\ndisplay, `error` if the last fetch attempt failed, or `success` if the query has data to display.\n`isPending`/`isSuccess`/`isError` are derived booleans for convenience.\n\n### See\n\n[queryOptions](../functions/queryOptions.md) to share these options between `useQuery` and imperative APIs like `queryClient.query`.\n\n### Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { For, Match, Switch } from 'solid-js'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Posts() {\n  const postsQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['posts'],\n    queryFn: fetchPosts,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Switch>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isPending}>Loading...</Match>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isError}>Error: {postsQuery.error.message}</Match>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isSuccess}>\n        <ul>\n          <For each={postsQuery.data}>{(post) => <li>{post.title}</li>}</For>\n        </ul>\n        <div>{postsQuery.isFetching ? 'Background Updating...' : ' '}</div>\n      </Match>\n    </Switch>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`select` derives whatever `data` a component needs from the cached value, without changing what's\nactually stored in the cache — the cache still holds the full `Post[]`, but `data` here is a `number`:\n```tsx\nimport { Match, Switch } from 'solid-js'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction PostCount() {\n  const postsQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['posts'],\n    queryFn: fetchPosts,\n    select: (posts) => posts.length,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Switch>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isPending}>Loading...</Match>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isError}>Error: {postsQuery.error.message}</Match>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isSuccess}>{postsQuery.data} posts</Match>\n    </Switch>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nA dependent query, only enabled once `postId` is set:\n```tsx\nimport { Match, Switch } from 'solid-js'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Post(props: { postId: number | undefined }) {\n  const postQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['post', props.postId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchPost(props.postId!),\n    enabled: props.postId != null,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Switch fallback={<h1>{postQuery.data?.title}</h1>}>\n      <Match when={props.postId == null}>Select a post</Match>\n      <Match when={postQuery.isLoading}>Loading...</Match>\n      <Match when={postQuery.isError}>Error: {postQuery.error.message}</Match>\n    </Switch>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe same dependent query, using `skipToken` to disable it in a type-safe way instead of relying on\n`enabled`. The non-null assertion is still needed — Solid's `props` narrowing doesn't survive into the\n`queryFn` closure the way a local `const` would — but `skipToken` keeps `queryFn`'s return type accurate\nwithout it. `refetch` doesn't work while `queryFn` is `skipToken` — use `enabled: false` instead if you\nneed to trigger the query manually:\n```tsx\nimport { Match, Switch } from 'solid-js'\nimport { skipToken, useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Post(props: { postId: number | undefined }) {\n  const postQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['post', props.postId],\n    queryFn: props.postId != null ? () => fetchPost(props.postId!) : skipToken,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Switch fallback={<h1>{postQuery.data?.title}</h1>}>\n      <Match when={props.postId == null}>Select a post</Match>\n      <Match when={postQuery.isLoading}>Loading...</Match>\n      <Match when={postQuery.isError}>Error: {postQuery.error.message}</Match>\n    </Switch>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nSeeding a detail query from an already-cached list, to skip the loading state. `initialDataUpdatedAt` carries\nover the list's own fetch time, so that if you set a `staleTime`, it's measured from when the list was\nfetched rather than from now:\n```tsx\nimport { useQuery, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Post(props: { postId: number }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n\n  const postQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['post', props.postId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchPost(props.postId),\n    initialData: () =>\n      queryClient\n        .getQueryData<Array<Post>>(['posts'])\n        ?.find((post) => post.id === props.postId),\n    initialDataUpdatedAt: () =>\n      queryClient.getQueryState(['posts'])?.dataUpdatedAt,\n  }))\n\n  return postQuery.isError ? <span>Error: {postQuery.error.message}</span> : <h1>{postQuery.data?.title}</h1>\n}\n```\n\nPaginated data, keeping the previous page's data visible while the next page loads:\n```tsx\nimport { For, createSignal } from 'solid-js'\nimport { keepPreviousData, useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Posts() {\n  const [page, setPage] = createSignal(0)\n\n  const postsQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['posts', page()],\n    queryFn: () => fetchPosts(page()),\n    placeholderData: keepPreviousData,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <ul>\n        <For each={postsQuery.data}>{(post) => <li>{post.title}</li>}</For>\n      </ul>\n      <button\n        disabled={postsQuery.isPlaceholderData}\n        onClick={() => setPage((old) => old + 1)}\n      >\n        Next Page\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Call Signature\n\n```ts\n<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>(options: DefinedInitialDataOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>, queryClient?: () => QueryClient): DefinedUseQueryResult<TData, TError>;\n```\n\nSubscribes to a query: a declarative dependency on an asynchronous source of data that is tied to a unique key.\nThe query runs when the options call for it — `enabled: false` skips the initial fetch.\n\nThis overload is selected when `initialData` is set, so the resulting `data` is never `undefined` (unless\na `select` changes `TData` to include `undefined`).\n\n### Type Parameters\n\n#### TQueryFnData\n\n`TQueryFnData` = `unknown`\n\n#### TError\n\n`TError` = `Error`\n\n#### TData\n\n`TData` = `TQueryFnData`\n\n#### TQueryKey\n\n`TQueryKey` *extends* readonly `unknown`[] = readonly `unknown`[]\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### options\n\n[`DefinedInitialDataOptions`](../type-aliases/DefinedInitialDataOptions.md)\\<`TQueryFnData`, `TError`, `TData`, `TQueryKey`\\>\n\nAn accessor returning the [DefinedInitialDataOptions](../type-aliases/DefinedInitialDataOptions.md) to use — everything you can\npass to `useQuery`, with `initialData` set.\n\n#### queryClient?\n\n() => [`QueryClient`](../classes/QueryClient.md)\n\nAn accessor for a custom `QueryClient`. Otherwise, the one from the nearest context\nwill be used.\n\n### Returns\n\n[`DefinedUseQueryResult`](../type-aliases/DefinedUseQueryResult.md)\\<`TData`, `TError`\\>\n\nThe current query result, as a Solid store, typed so that `status` is `success` — or `error` if a\nfetch attempt fails while keeping the existing data (`status` never resolves to `pending` in this overload's\ntype, since `initialData` guarantees data upfront). `isSuccess`/`isError` are derived booleans for\nconvenience.\n\n### See\n\n[queryOptions](../functions/queryOptions.md) to share these options between `useQuery` and imperative APIs like `queryClient.query`.\n\n### Example\n\n```tsx\nimport { For } from 'solid-js'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Posts() {\n  // `postsQuery.data` is never `undefined`, thanks to `initialData` — even if a refetch fails, so the\n  // list stays visible alongside the error.\n  const postsQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['posts'],\n    queryFn: fetchPosts,\n    initialData: [],\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {postsQuery.isError ? <span>Error: {postsQuery.error.message}</span> : null}\n      <ul>\n        <For each={postsQuery.data}>{(post) => <li>{post.title}</li>}</For>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createQuery\ntitle: createQuery\n---\n\n```ts\nconst createQuery: {\n<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>  (options: UndefinedInitialDataOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>, queryClient?: () => QueryClient): UseQueryResult<TData, TError>;\n<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>  (options: DefinedInitialDataOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>, queryClient?: () => QueryClient): DefinedUseQueryResult<TData, TError>;\n} = useQuery;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/solid-query/src/index.ts:57](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/solid-query/src/index.ts#L57)\n\n## Call Signature\n\n```ts\n<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>(options: UndefinedInitialDataOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>, queryClient?: () => QueryClient): UseQueryResult<TData, TError>;\n```\n\nSubscribes to a query: a declarative dependency on an asynchronous source of data that is tied to a unique key.\nThe query runs when the options call for it — `enabled: false` skips the initial fetch.\n\n### Type Parameters\n\n#### TQueryFnData\n\n`TQueryFnData` = `unknown`\n\n#### TError\n\n`TError` = `Error`\n\n#### TData\n\n`TData` = `TQueryFnData`\n\n#### TQueryKey\n\n`TQueryKey` *extends* readonly `unknown`[] = readonly `unknown`[]\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### options\n\n[`UndefinedInitialDataOptions`](../type-aliases/UndefinedInitialDataOptions.md)\\<`TQueryFnData`, `TError`, `TData`, `TQueryKey`\\>\n\nAn accessor returning the [UndefinedInitialDataOptions](../type-aliases/UndefinedInitialDataOptions.md) to use — everything you can\npass to `useQuery`.\n\n#### queryClient?\n\n() => [`QueryClient`](../classes/QueryClient.md)\n\nAn accessor for a custom `QueryClient`. Otherwise, the one from the nearest context\nwill be used.\n\n### Returns\n\n[`UseQueryResult`](../type-aliases/UseQueryResult.md)\\<`TData`, `TError`\\>\n\nThe current query result, as a Solid store. `status` is `pending` if there is no cached data to\ndisplay, `error` if the last fetch attempt failed, or `success` if the query has data to display.\n`isPending`/`isSuccess`/`isError` are derived booleans for convenience.\n\n### See\n\n[queryOptions](../functions/queryOptions.md) to share these options between `useQuery` and imperative APIs like `queryClient.query`.\n\n### Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { For, Match, Switch } from 'solid-js'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Posts() {\n  const postsQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['posts'],\n    queryFn: fetchPosts,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Switch>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isPending}>Loading...</Match>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isError}>Error: {postsQuery.error.message}</Match>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isSuccess}>\n        <ul>\n          <For each={postsQuery.data}>{(post) => <li>{post.title}</li>}</For>\n        </ul>\n        <div>{postsQuery.isFetching ? 'Background Updating...' : ' '}</div>\n      </Match>\n    </Switch>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`select` derives whatever `data` a component needs from the cached value, without changing what's\nactually stored in the cache — the cache still holds the full `Post[]`, but `data` here is a `number`:\n```tsx\nimport { Match, Switch } from 'solid-js'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction PostCount() {\n  const postsQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['posts'],\n    queryFn: fetchPosts,\n    select: (posts) => posts.length,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Switch>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isPending}>Loading...</Match>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isError}>Error: {postsQuery.error.message}</Match>\n      <Match when={postsQuery.isSuccess}>{postsQuery.data} posts</Match>\n    </Switch>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nA dependent query, only enabled once `postId` is set:\n```tsx\nimport { Match, Switch } from 'solid-js'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Post(props: { postId: number | undefined }) {\n  const postQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['post', props.postId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchPost(props.postId!),\n    enabled: props.postId != null,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Switch fallback={<h1>{postQuery.data?.title}</h1>}>\n      <Match when={props.postId == null}>Select a post</Match>\n      <Match when={postQuery.isLoading}>Loading...</Match>\n      <Match when={postQuery.isError}>Error: {postQuery.error.message}</Match>\n    </Switch>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe same dependent query, using `skipToken` to disable it in a type-safe way instead of relying on\n`enabled`. The non-null assertion is still needed — Solid's `props` narrowing doesn't survive into the\n`queryFn` closure the way a local `const` would — but `skipToken` keeps `queryFn`'s return type accurate\nwithout it. `refetch` doesn't work while `queryFn` is `skipToken` — use `enabled: false` instead if you\nneed to trigger the query manually:\n```tsx\nimport { Match, Switch } from 'solid-js'\nimport { skipToken, useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Post(props: { postId: number | undefined }) {\n  const postQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['post', props.postId],\n    queryFn: props.postId != null ? () => fetchPost(props.postId!) : skipToken,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <Switch fallback={<h1>{postQuery.data?.title}</h1>}>\n      <Match when={props.postId == null}>Select a post</Match>\n      <Match when={postQuery.isLoading}>Loading...</Match>\n      <Match when={postQuery.isError}>Error: {postQuery.error.message}</Match>\n    </Switch>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nSeeding a detail query from an already-cached list, to skip the loading state. `initialDataUpdatedAt` carries\nover the list's own fetch time, so that if you set a `staleTime`, it's measured from when the list was\nfetched rather than from now:\n```tsx\nimport { useQuery, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Post(props: { postId: number }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n\n  const postQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['post', props.postId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchPost(props.postId),\n    initialData: () =>\n      queryClient\n        .getQueryData<Array<Post>>(['posts'])\n        ?.find((post) => post.id === props.postId),\n    initialDataUpdatedAt: () =>\n      queryClient.getQueryState(['posts'])?.dataUpdatedAt,\n  }))\n\n  return postQuery.isError ? <span>Error: {postQuery.error.message}</span> : <h1>{postQuery.data?.title}</h1>\n}\n```\n\nPaginated data, keeping the previous page's data visible while the next page loads:\n```tsx\nimport { For, createSignal } from 'solid-js'\nimport { keepPreviousData, useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Posts() {\n  const [page, setPage] = createSignal(0)\n\n  const postsQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['posts', page()],\n    queryFn: () => fetchPosts(page()),\n    placeholderData: keepPreviousData,\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <ul>\n        <For each={postsQuery.data}>{(post) => <li>{post.title}</li>}</For>\n      </ul>\n      <button\n        disabled={postsQuery.isPlaceholderData}\n        onClick={() => setPage((old) => old + 1)}\n      >\n        Next Page\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Call Signature\n\n```ts\n<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>(options: DefinedInitialDataOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>, queryClient?: () => QueryClient): DefinedUseQueryResult<TData, TError>;\n```\n\nSubscribes to a query: a declarative dependency on an asynchronous source of data that is tied to a unique key.\nThe query runs when the options call for it — `enabled: false` skips the initial fetch.\n\nThis overload is selected when `initialData` is set, so the resulting `data` is never `undefined` (unless\na `select` changes `TData` to include `undefined`).\n\n### Type Parameters\n\n#### TQueryFnData\n\n`TQueryFnData` = `unknown`\n\n#### TError\n\n`TError` = `Error`\n\n#### TData\n\n`TData` = `TQueryFnData`\n\n#### TQueryKey\n\n`TQueryKey` *extends* readonly `unknown`[] = readonly `unknown`[]\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### options\n\n[`DefinedInitialDataOptions`](../type-aliases/DefinedInitialDataOptions.md)\\<`TQueryFnData`, `TError`, `TData`, `TQueryKey`\\>\n\nAn accessor returning the [DefinedInitialDataOptions](../type-aliases/DefinedInitialDataOptions.md) to use — everything you can\npass to `useQuery`, with `initialData` set.\n\n#### queryClient?\n\n() => [`QueryClient`](../classes/QueryClient.md)\n\nAn accessor for a custom `QueryClient`. Otherwise, the one from the nearest context\nwill be used.\n\n### Returns\n\n[`DefinedUseQueryResult`](../type-aliases/DefinedUseQueryResult.md)\\<`TData`, `TError`\\>\n\nThe current query result, as a Solid store, typed so that `status` is `success` — or `error` if a\nfetch attempt fails while keeping the existing data (`status` never resolves to `pending` in this overload's\ntype, since `initialData` guarantees data upfront). `isSuccess`/`isError` are derived booleans for\nconvenience.\n\n### See\n\n[queryOptions](../functions/queryOptions.md) to share these options between `useQuery` and imperative APIs like `queryClient.query`.\n\n### Example\n\n```tsx\nimport { For } from 'solid-js'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction Posts() {\n  // `postsQuery.data` is never `undefined`, thanks to `initialData` — even if a refetch fails, so the\n  // list stays visible alongside the error.\n  const postsQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['posts'],\n    queryFn: fetchPosts,\n    initialData: [],\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {postsQuery.isError ? <span>Error: {postsQuery.error.message}</span> : null}\n      <ul>\n        <For each={postsQuery.data}>{(post) => <li>{post.title}</li>}</For>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
